#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-capture-helper: the work behind Hearth Capture (Capture.qml), Hearth's own screenshot tool (1.14; it
replaces KDE's Spectacle in Desktop Mode). The window, the area picker and the markup editor are QML; this takes the
picture, keeps the recent ones, copies, reads text and QR codes, and opens the folder.

  hearth-capture-helper tools                       JSON: what this PC has (grim, KWin, tesseract, zbarimg, wl-copy, recorder)
  hearth-capture-helper grab MODE [--screen NAME] [--geometry X,Y,W,H] [--pointer]
                                                    take a picture: MODE all | screen | window | area. JSON {ok, path}
                                                    or {ok: false, pick: true} when this compositor can't find the
                                                    window by itself (labwc): the area picker is used instead
  hearth-capture-helper grab-each [--pointer] NAME...  the area picker's still pictures: one per screen, JSON {ok, shots}
  hearth-capture-helper put                         the editor's finished picture (PNG, JPEG or WEBP in base64 on standard
                                                    input) to a new file of its own: JSON {ok, path, width, height, kind}
  hearth-capture-helper save SRC [--to PATH] [--replace]
                                                    keep SRC in Pictures/Screenshots ("Screenshot 2026-11-16 21-04-05.png",
                                                    " (2)" for a second one that second) or at PATH (Save as: never over
                                                    a file that's there unless --replace; the picture's kind must match
                                                    PATH's ending), and in the recent list
  hearth-capture-helper copy PATH                   the picture to the clipboard (wl-copy)
  hearth-capture-helper copy-text                   standard input to the clipboard (recognised text, a QR code's text)
  hearth-capture-helper history                     JSON {items}: recent captures, newest first, only files still there
  hearth-capture-helper forget PATH                 take one off the recent list (the file stays)
  hearth-capture-helper trash PATH                  move the file to the Trash and take it off the list
  hearth-capture-helper ocr PATH [--lang eng]       JSON {ok, text} (tesseract), or {ok: false, missing: "tesseract"}
  hearth-capture-helper qr PATH                     JSON {ok, codes} (zbarimg), or {ok: false, missing: "zbarimg"}
  hearth-capture-helper folder PATH                 show the file in Hearth Files
  hearth-capture-helper record                      start or stop the screen recorder (hearth-record, else Hearth Recorder)
  hearth-capture-helper clean                       remove the editor's own temporary pictures older than a day
  hearth-capture-helper scroll --geometry X,Y,W,H [--auto] [--pointer]
                                                    scrolling capture (1.14): pictures of that area one after another
                                                    while it scrolls (by itself with --auto: the mouse wheel, through
                                                    a virtual mouse; or as you scroll it), stitched into one long
                                                    picture where each new one overlaps the last. Until it reaches the
                                                    end, `scroll-stop`, or the limits. JSON {ok, path, width, height,
                                                    frames, why} ({ok: false, cancelled: true} after scroll-stop --cancel)
  hearth-capture-helper scroll-stop [--cancel]      finish the scrolling capture now (or throw it away)
  hearth-capture-helper apps                        JSON {apps}: the apps that open pictures, for Share › Open with
  hearth-capture-helper open-with APP PATH          open the picture in APP (its .desktop id)
  hearth-capture-helper phones                      JSON {on, phones}: Phone link's connected phones (hearth-phone)
  hearth-capture-helper send-phone PATH ID          send the picture to phone ID (Phone link's share)

The recent list is state, not a setting: ~/.local/state/nimbus/capture-history.json, written through
hearth_settings_io (lock, atomic, .bak). Capture's own choices (mode, delay, pointer) are in ~/.config/nimbus/
capture.json, written by Capture.qml through SettingsWriter, only when you change one.

Taking the picture is one function, grab(), so the way it's done can be swapped in one place:
  1. hearth-screens (next to this file, from feature/kwin-screens): `grab MODE [--screen N] [--geometry X,Y,W,H]
     [--pointer] --out FILE`, on both compositors;
  2. a grim-compatible tool: /usr/bin/hearth-screenshot under KWin (HEARTH_WM=kwin), grim on labwc.
Output: one JSON line. Nothing here ever reads or keeps a password.
"""
